(footprint "U9_SOT23_5"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "solar-glow-drh")
	(generator_version "1.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "SOT-23-5 (JEDEC MO-178 Var AA), 2.90x1.60mm body, 0.95mm pitch. Land geometry carried over verbatim from the SOT-23-6 pattern this project routed U9 against, MINUS the vacant middle land on the two-lead side -- so pad positions are bit-identical to the routed board and no trace moves. Numbering is the standard 5-pin one: pads 1/2/3 down one side, pad 4 opposite pad 3, PAD 5 OPPOSITE PAD 1. That last point is the whole reason this footprint exists: on a SOT-23-6 land the OUT lead of a 5-pin part falls on pad 6, not pad 5, which silently left VS unconnected. For TPS7A0233PDBVR (and any 5-pin SOT-23).")
	(tags "SOT-23-5 SOT23 TPS7A02 LDO")
